Journey: The PostgreSQL customer ledger matches the shop
Tags: @postgres @db @api
Risk: 3

# API <-> DB: the shop's customers API and the ledger agree, column by column (numeric comes back as "25000.00")
Call API "GET /api/customers" as manager and store as customers
Expect the customers response status is 200
Run query "LEDGER_CUSTOMERS" on ledger and store the rows as ledger
Compare ${customers.body} with ${ledger} by id

# Named binds (:name -> $n), a fragment, a typed default and PostgreSQL casts (::numeric, ::date)
Expect query "CUSTOMERS_BY_REGION" on ledger with region="EU" returns 2 rows
Expect query "CUSTOMERS_BY_REGION" on ledger with region="EU", min_limit=20000 returns 1 row
Get the value of query "CUSTOMER_NAME" with id=${customers.body.1.id} as secondName
Expect ${secondName} equals "Fabrikam Inc"

# PostgreSQL syntax: random(), LIMIT, CURRENT_DATE
Get the first row of query "RANDOM_ACTIVE_CUSTOMER" as pick
Expect len(pick.customer_name) > 0
Expect query "CUSTOMERS_ONBOARDED_SINCE" with since="2024-06-01" returns 2 rows
Wait until query "LEDGER_CUSTOMER_COUNT" on ledger returns 1 row within 5 seconds

# UI <-> DB: the customer picked from the ledger is offered on the order form
Log in as manager
Open /orders/new
Expect the page contains "${pick.customer_name}"
